{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Esav saw that they were evil, etc.</b> The verse tells us that Esav was mindful only of his father's disapproval of them, but apart from that, as for the fact that they are of the aspect of evil, he was not mindful — his soul does not recoil from them. And from this you may also infer that the reason that they were evil in the eyes of Yitzchak availed only to prevent him from adding more of them, but to divorce those who were already with him — no. Or perhaps all his feeling was nothing but concern lest his blessings be diminished on account of the children who would be born to him from the daughters of Canaan; therefore he took from the daughters of Yishmael, so that the blessings would be fulfilled through the intermediary of the children who would be born to him from them." "<b>Thus concludes the portion of Toldot.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:11.313540136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}